# The image build sends this whole directory to the Docker daemon as the build context. Nothing in
# examples/gaia2/cli/Dockerfile copies a secret into a layer — every COPY names an explicit path —
# but the context itself is worth keeping clean: a later `COPY . ` would otherwise bake whatever is
# sitting in the working tree into the image, and `.env` holds real API keys.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never needed by the build, and large: uploading them slows every build for nothing.
.git/
.venv/
venv/
.claude/
notes/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
site/
